Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
**412 reports** merged into #4471. They are not one bug. They are **two problems**, and each now has its own ticket.

<Callout>
Not "known, one fix queued". The parser fix covers 379 of the 412 reports. The other 33 need a different fix.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
|---|---|---|
| Shared parser reads dates month first, so day-first tenants get month and day flipped (`parser`) | **379** | [issue 1](https://github.com/rvazquezglez/what-it-shows-4471/issues/1) |
| booking-v3 form hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, who type month first (`hint`) | **33** | [issue 2](https://github.com/rvazquezglez/what-it-shows-4471/issues/2) |

379 + 33 = 412. The count includes 5 reports the desk notes read as a one-day move (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). They are filed under `parser` by tenant, as the table below shows.

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the browser. 15 of the 33 `hint` reports were tagged `parser`.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Merging on subject line hid three causes under one count. Check the cause before you merge.
- Write the page while the queue is still in your head.

